# fixedbugs, defect 2318, 2026-11-07: beside the issue's shapes, N
# parameters and N sibling blocks each binding `y`. The resolver's map named
# the place the block before had bound `y` at, which that block's closing
# took away, so each `y` after the first scanned every open binding to learn
# that none held it. A closing scope now gives each name it took away the
# place it stood over. The compiler's own instructions checking N of each at
# 2,048, 4,096 and 8,192: 5.11, 12.94 and 37.09 billion before, 3.71, 7.35
# and 14.59 after. This case, 2,048 of each and one binding that shadows the
# first parameter, told naming its line: 4.04 billion before, 2.65 after.
